Swipe Keyboard licences

This project follows KDE's licensing policy (https://community.kde.org/Policies/Licensing_Policy) and the REUSE
specification (https://reuse.software): every file names its copyright holders and licence, either in an SPDX header
or in REUSE.toml, and the full licence texts are in LICENSES/.

- Keyboard plugin, QML, integration, tools, scripts and tests: GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only OR
  LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL (you may use the GNU GPL version 2 or version 3, or a later version accepted by KDE e.V.).
- Engine library (engine/: swipe recognition, dictionary, prediction): LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR
  LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL.
- CMake build files: BSD-3-Clause.
- Documentation and images: CC-BY-SA-4.0. Trivial or generated data: CC0-1.0.
- Data files keep their own licences: word lists and language packs ODC-By-1.0 and CC BY 2.0 France (Tatoeba), the
  AOSP word list Apache-2.0, the swear-word lists CC-BY-4.0, the texting-word lists CC0-1.0, the trained models as
  declared in their release (see packaging/NOTICE and packaging/language-models/README.md).

